  "sourceFindings": [
    "The pinned to-do documentation provides a desktop New to-do entry above the list. Its ordering prose is internally inconsistent; sorting remains outside this feature.",
    "Note.newTodo calls Note.new(parentId) then sets is_todo=true; Note.new preserves the selected parent and obtains remaining defaults from its superclass.",
    "The desktop newTodo command delegates newNote(body,true). newNote uses the valid active folder, is_todo1, the supplied body and provisional:true, then selects and sorts the saved item.",
    "The desktop enabled condition requires one valid selected folder outside conflict/read-only/trash. The candidate draft permits explicit notebook choice and defaults to Notes, a disclosed policy difference."
  ],
  "candidateContract": [
    "New to-do chooses an unsaved draft type; no mutation or provisional record occurs until explicit Save.",
    "A new save may carry newTodo:true; only Boolean values are accepted and existing-note saves must omit the flag. Saved-note type changes keep their existing endpoints.",
    "Snapshot caller fields before waiting on the queue; validate and bind notebook in cloned state, then make one state commit containing both note and to-do fields.",
    "Revision1 creation starts open with due0/completed0/history0. Ordinary later saves preserve to-do state and build bounded history; cold restart and JEX preserve supported metadata.",
    "One pending save blocks duplicate saves, preserves newer typed body at the returned revision, and respects a newer editor or disposed view after real commit or failure.",
    "After actual save commit, a later list-refresh failure is a separate outcome. Its message may publish only while the accepted generation, draft revision and all current field values still match; newer typing keeps its unsaved status and next save uses the committed ID/revision."
  ],
